    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) stands as our clear anchor, benefiting from an elite park factor and a favorable matchup against Baz, whose 4.62 xERA presents a prime opportunity to drive in runs. **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) provides the next highest ceiling; despite facing a lefty, his strong platoon dynamic and a favorable #2 order slot keep him locked in as a high-efficiency start. Meanwhile, our speed-focused strategy is highlighted by **Mickey Moniak** (69.47) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.54). **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing today; his 14% platoon boost combined with the pitcher's slow delivery speed makes him a top-tier threat to swipe a bag, a critical factor given our aggressive prioritization of stolen base upside.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion of the day was **Kyle Karros**, whose 46.70 score fell just short of the threshold. While he benefits from the same favorable slow-delivery matchup as **Mickey Moniak**, his lack of a strong platoon advantage and a lower batting order placement relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-floor options like **James Wood** (66.26), who enters the day with an elite 0.434 xwOBA. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Brice Turang** (45.98) and **Jose Caballero** (45.56); both face tough pitching assignments against Skenes and Cavalli respectively. **Brice Turang** in particular faces a steep 19% SP skill penalty, further compounded by the catcher\u2019s elite pop time, making his stolen base potential significantly harder to realize today. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as any late-breaking weather or shifts in confirmed order could necessitate a quick pivot for our marginal starts.",
